{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "name": "Catamaran",
  "notes": "Two hulls and a footbridge. Each hull is a whole ship — core, gun, engines — and what joins them is four sections of thin structure, so the pair is held together by welds a fraction of the width of the ones inside either hull. Built to be cut in half: what the two halves then do is what tells you whether a piece with a core of its own is a ship or wreckage.",
